Sval: a page's embed observer rescans only for an embed it was given

The embed shims' MutationObserver passes every added element's
querySelectorAll result to createShimPlaceholders, which reads an empty
list as "search the whole document". Allowing a page's embeds puts one
shim's embed back, the other shim's observer rescans, and the rescan
searches only after awaiting the add-on's strings, by which time that
shim's own unblock has put its embed back. The embed just allowed gets
its placeholder again.

diff --git a/browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/smartblock_embeds_helper.js b/browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/smartblock_embeds_helper.js
index 1d2f6e170c..f561c1da04 100644
--- a/browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/smartblock_embeds_helper.js
+++ b/browser/extensions/webcompat/lib/smartblock_embeds_helper.js
@@ -411,7 +411,7 @@ const embedHelperLib = (() => {
             // If element is not an embed, check if any children are
             // and replace if needed
             let maybeEmbedNodeList = node.querySelectorAll?.(embedSelector);
-            if (maybeEmbedNodeList) {
+            if (maybeEmbedNodeList?.length) {
               createShimPlaceholders(maybeEmbedNodeList, SHIM_INFO);
             }
           }
